Subject: Makefile-libbz2_so: add -lc to the -shared link

Substrate's cross-ld elf_i386_substrate emulation only emits a
.dynamic section (PT_DYNAMIC + DT_HASH + DT_STRTAB + ...) when the
link line pulls in at least one DT_NEEDED — passing only object
files produces an ET_DYN with NO dynamic-linking metadata, which
the substrate ld.so can't load.

Adding -lc makes the link explicitly NEEDED on libc.so.0; that
nudges the linker into laying down PT_DYNAMIC and produces a
proper shared library.  Same shape as the workaround OpenSSL uses
(LDFLAGS=-lc).

---
diff -urN a/Makefile-libbz2_so b/Makefile-libbz2_so
--- a/Makefile-libbz2_so
+++ b/Makefile-libbz2_so
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
       bzlib.o

 all: $(OBJS)
-	$(CC) -shared -Wl,-soname -Wl,libbz2.so.1.0 -o libbz2.so.1.0.8 $(OBJS)
+	$(CC) -shared -Wl,-soname -Wl,libbz2.so.1.0 -o libbz2.so.1.0.8 $(OBJS) -lc
 	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -o bzip2-shared bzip2.c libbz2.so.1.0.8
 	rm -f libbz2.so.1.0
 	rm -f libbz2.so.1
